{title: 291 - We Have Not Known Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #291 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 291}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db/Ab]We have not known [Ebm/Gb]Thee [Db/F]as [Ab]we [Db/Ab]ought,
[Ab]Nor learned Thy wisdom, grace, [Db/Ab]and [Bbm]power;
[Ab7/Gb]The [Gb]things [Ab7/Gb]of [Db/F]earth have [Ebm]filed [E/B]our [Bbm]thoughts,
[Bbm/F]And trifles of [Ebm/Bb]the passing [Gb]hour.
[Db/F]Lord, give us [Ab]light Thy [Db/Ab]truth [Ebm/Gb]to [Db/F]see,
[Gb]And [Fm]make [Ebm]us [Db]wise in [Bbm]knowing [Gb]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db/Ab]We have not feared [Ebm/Gb]Thee [Db/F]as [Ab]we [Db/Ab]ought,
[Ab]Nor bowed beneath [Bbm]Thine [Ab]awful [Bbm]eye,
[Ab7/Gb]Nor [Gb]guarded [Db/F]deed, and [Ebm]word, [E/B]and [Bbm]thought,
[Bbm/F]Remembering [Ebm/Bb]that God [Ab]was [Gb]nigh.
[Db/F]Lord, give us [Ab]faith to [Db/Ab]know [Ebm/Gb]Thee [Db/F]near,
[Gb]And [Fm]grant [Ebm]the [Db]grace of [Bbm]holy [Gb]fear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db/Ab]We have not loved [Ebm/Gb]Thee [Db/F]as [Ab]we [Db/Ab]ought,
[Ab]Nor cared that we [Bbm]are [Ab]loved [Db/Ab]by [Bbm]Thee;
[Ab7/Gb]Thy [Gb]presence [Db/F]we have [Ebm]coldly [Bbm]sought,
[Bbm/F]And feebly longed [Ebm/Bb]Thy face [Ab]to [Gb]see.
[Db/F]Lord, give a [Ab]pure and [Db/Ab]loving heart
[Gb]To [Fm]feel [Ebm]and [Db]own the [Bbm]love [Ab]Thou [Gb]art.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Db/Ab]We have not served [Ebm/Gb]Thee [Db/F]as [Ab]we [Db/Ab]ought;
[Ab]Alas! the duties left [Db/Ab]undone,
[Ab7/Gb]The [Gb]work [Ab7/Gb]with [Db/F]little [Ebm]fervor [Bbm]wrought,
[Bbm/F]The battles lost, [Ebm/Bb]or scarcely won!
[Db/F]Lord, give the [Ab]zeal, and [Db/Ab]give [Ebm/Gb]the [Db/F]might,
[Gb]For [Fm]Thee [Ebm]to [Db]toil, for [Bbm]Thee [Ab]to [Gb]fight.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Db/Ab]When shall we know [Ebm/Gb]Thee [Db/F]as [Ab]we [Db/Ab]ought,
[Ab]And fear, and love, [Bbm]and [Ab]serve [Db/Ab]aright!
[Ab7/Gb]When [Gb]shall [Ab7/Gb]we, [Ab]out [Db]of [E/B]trial [Bbm]brought,
[Bbm/F]Be perfect in [Ebm/Bb]the land [Ab]of [Gb]light!
[Db/F]Lord, may we [Ab]day by [Db/Ab]day [Ebm/Gb]prepare
[Gb]To [Fm]see [Ebm]Thy [Db]face, and [Bbm]serve [Ab]Thee [Gb]there.
{end_of_verse}
